  "title": "Computer vision & perception meetup",
  "date": "2026-07-01T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Computer vision & perception meetup\n\nposter\n\nMy first train trip in Estonia\n\nI don't know that the train is free in Tallinn area. Since I live in Tondi now, I can take the train to the city centre.\n\nTondi\n\nTrain\n\nOld Town\n\nTopics\n\nWhy computer vision for Human well-being monitoring is hard.\n\nHe mentioned that he uses thermal camera instead of rgb camera in case of the fear of privacy concerns. My personal view, even it is a thermal camera, it is still a camera. People are still worry about it. It is the network safety should be worried about.\n\nML for Vision and Sensing in Muon Tomography\n\nThis is an interesting one. Muon is a space ray that can run across objects. It can be used to scan an object and see what is inside. They used 3D U-Net to show the item.\n\nlightcode photonics\n\nThey shared the bit code way to support different coordinate system in 3D engines.\n\nOn SLAM: ARAEL optimization framework\n\nARAEL\n\nIt is an implementation of SLAM (Simultaneous location and mapping) in Rust. Well, since it is for training, I think it is better using python.\nThe memory safety feature of rust is totally not used in the project and many unsafe code.\n\nWearable cameras as behavioral analytics\n\nThis is an idea sharing, something like AI pin.\n\nA Unified Multimodal Perception Module for Contextual Understanding\n\nThis is a robot with many sensors and cameras to mimic environment sensing.\n\nsystem pipeline",
